{=============================================================================
  Full-power operating point of a 4-stroke gas engine, combustion products
  described by their mean specific heat cpbar
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0034
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Steady-state model of the whole engine at its nominal point, as in the
  original exercise (ULiege MSTh repetition, TP 08, exercise 4 of 2005-11-14):

  - states 1 to 5 (as in the original): the charge flow rate is fixed by the
    displaced volume flow V_dot_4 = i*N_rot*ncVs; from state 2 an isentropic
    path (s_2) to the pressure P_3 = p_4, with the kinetic-energy balance
    c_p_2*(t_2 - t_3) = C_3^2/2 and V_dot_3 = A_3*C_3, closes the intake
    pressure P_2; the original introduces an intake pressure loss ('throttle
    of the carburettor') that brings the shaft power to zero;
  - combustion: an energy balance between the reactants (air and methane
    brought to the reference temperature 25 C) and the combustion products,
    whose mean specific heat is given by the cpbar routine of the ULiege
    combustion library between 25 C and t_6 (adiabatic flame temperature);
  - expansion: W_dot_sh = M_dot_g*c_p_g_67*(t_6 - t_7) between t_6 and t_7, the
    mean specific heat of the products between t_6 and t_7 being computed by
    cpbar again (W_dot_sh = 0 imposed: t_7 = t_6);
  - cooling: the products are cooled by the engine jacket (eps-NTU, AU_gw) down
    to t_8, and the cooling water rejects Q_dot_gw and Q_dot_wa to the
    environment (eps-NTU, AU_wa).

  Simplified air (79 % N2, 21 % O2) is used in cpbar; CH4 is the fuel; the
  incomplete-combustion branch (CO losses) exists in cpbar but is not used here
  (air excess e > 0).

  Inputs : AU_gw, AU_wa        conductance products of the jacket and of the
                               water-to-environment exchanger [W/K]
           A_3, ncVs, i, rpm   area A_3 [m^2], displacement ncVs [m^3],
                               working cycles per revolution [-], speed [rpm]
           eta_in_act, T_m     actual indicated efficiency [-], torque [N.m]
           f, LHV, m, n        fuel-air ratio [kg/kg], lower heating value
                               [J/kg], CmHn formula of the fuel [-]
           t_a, p              ambient air temperature [C], pressure [Pa]
           M_dot_w, t_w_su     cooling water flow [kg/s] and supply temp. [C]
  Outputs: P_2                 intake pressure after the throttle [Pa] (solved)
           t_6, t_7, t_8       flame, exhaust and jacket-out temperatures [C]
           M_dot_a, M_dot_f     air and fuel mass flow rates [kg/s]
           Q_dot_1..Q_dot_5     combustion-side heat terms [W]
           Q_dot_gw, Q_dot_wa   cooling-side powers [W]
           W_dot_in_act, eta_sh  indicated power [W] and shaft efficiency [-]
  Units  : SI - temperatures in C, pressures in Pa, energies in J
  Source : ULiege MSTh exercise TP 08 Ex 4 (2005-11-14),
           ~/Nextcloud/thermo_models/machines et systemes thermiques/
           MSTh - Repetitions/TP 08/MSTH051114 EXERCICE 4.EES (TM-0127);
           EES version X7.458 - see README.md
  Status : verified against the stored EES solution of the original.
           Solve with the shipped .initials (the unknown flame temperature sits
           inside the cpbar calls).
 =============================================================================}
{--- Library functions copied from CSL-0005 (cpbar_combustion_products) ---
  Copied verbatim (P. Ngendakumana, ULiege 2003) until
  $INCLUDE library:cpbar_combustion_products is available (CS-FEAT-IMPORT).
  Only the cpbar PROCEDURE is needed by this model.}

PROCEDURE cpbar(m,n,f,T_p1,T_p2:c_bar_p,Q_4,x,e_min,e)

{CPBAR procedure returns cp_bar (J/kg.K) of the combustion products of a CmHn
hydrocarbon between two temperatures. The inputs are : the type of fuel (m and n),
the fuel-air ratio (f) and  the two temperatures (T_p1 and T_p2) in °C.

In the case of incomplete combustion (negative excess air value), the procedure
returns also : the energy losses by CO (Q_4 in J/kg of fuel), the fraction (x) of C
atoms oxidized into CO2 and the mininum excess air (e_min) to get x>0.

Simplified air is used. In the case of incomplete combustion, it is also assumed that
there is no O2 in the combustion products.

Moreover, the procedure returns the specific heat for pure air if f=0 (whatever m and n).

When using this procedure, don't forget to set mass basis calculation in the unit system
settings.}

"Check of the units setting"
IF (unitsystem('K')=1)  THEN CALL error('Please, set °C for temperature units!')
If (unitsystem('Molar')=1)  then CALL error('Please, set Mass basis!')

"Default values (in the case of complete combustion)"
Q_4 = 0
x = 1
e_min = 0
e = 0

"Composition of simplified air"
x_air_N2 = 0.79 ; x_air_O2= 0.21

"Universal gas constant"
R_u = 8314 "J/kmol.K"

"Molar masses of the species"
MM_CO = molarmass(CO) ; MM_N2 = molarmass(N2) ; MM_O2 = molarmass(O2)
MM_CO2 = molarmass(CO2) ; MM_H2O = molarmass(H2O)

IF (f>0) Then "combustion products (not pure air)"

"f  stoichiometric, excess air and f"
parfuel = m+n/4
MM_f = 12*m+1*n
f_st = MM_f/(parfuel*(MM_O2+(x_air_N2/x_air_O2)*MM_N2))
e = (f_st/f)-1

IF (f>f_st) Then "air deficiency"

"Stoichiometric combustion : CmHn+(m+n/4)*(O2+(79/21)*N2"
e_min = -m/(2*parfuel) "to ensure x>0"
f_max = f_st/(1+e_min)

"Assumption : enough air to oxidize H to H2O and no O2 in the flue gases"
"Hence : CmHn+(m+n/4)*(O2+(79/21)*N2)*(1+e) = a*CO2+b*CO+c*H2O+g*N2"
g = parfuel*(1+e)*(79/21)
c = n/2
x=2*(e*parfuel+m/2)/m
a = m*x "x is the fraction of the C atoms oxidized into CO2"
b = m*(1-x)
"Molar fractions of the constituents"
nkmoltot = a+ b + c +g
x_CO2 = a/nkmoltot
x_CO = b/nkmoltot
x_H2O = c/nkmoltot
x_N2 = g/nkmoltot
mmprod = x_CO2*MM_CO2+x_CO*MM_CO+x_H2O*MM_H2O+x_N2*MM_N2
"!Mean c_p of combustion products"
h_CO2 = (enthalpy(CO2,T=T_p1)-enthalpy(CO2,T=T_p2))*MM_CO2
h_CO = (enthalpy(CO,T=T_p1)-enthalpy(CO,T=T_p2))*MM_CO
h_H2O =(enthalpy(H2O,T=T_p1)-enthalpy(H2O,T=T_p2))*MM_H2O
h_N2 = (enthalpy(N2,T=T_p1)-enthalpy(N2,T=T_p2))*MM_N2
c_bar_p = ((x_CO2*h_CO2+x_CO*h_CO+x_H2O*h_H2O+x_N2*h_N2)/mmprod)/(T_p1-T_p2)

"Unburned-CO losses per kmol of fuel"
T_ref = 25
LHV_CO_mol = enthalpy(CO,T=T_ref)*MM_CO+0.5*enthalpy(O2,T=T_ref)*MM_O2-ENTHALPY(CO2,T=T_ref)*MM_CO2
LHV_CO_mas = LHV_CO_mol/MM_CO
Q_4 = LHV_CO_mol*b

ELSE

"Molar fractions of the constituents"
nkmoltot = m+ n/2 + parfuel*(e+(1+e)*(x_air_N2/x_air_O2))
x_CO2 = m/nkmoltot
x_H2O = (n/2)/nkmoltot
x_O2 = parfuel*e/nkmoltot
x_N2 = parfuel*(1+e)*(x_air_N2/x_air_O2)/nkmoltot

"Molar mass of combustion products"
MM_prod = x_CO2*MM_CO2+x_H2O*MM_H2O+x_O2*MM_O2+x_N2*MM_N2

"Enthalpy and mean specific heat of combustion products [per kg of products]"
hp_1 = (enthalpy(CO2,T=T_p1)-enthalpy(CO2, T=T_p2))*MM_CO2
hp_2 = (enthalpy(H2O,T=T_p1)-enthalpy(H2O, T=T_p2))*MM_H2O
hp_3 = (enthalpy(O2,T=T_p1)-enthalpy(O2, T=T_p2))*MM_O2
hp_4 = (enthalpy(N2,T=T_p1)-enthalpy(N2, T=T_p2))*MM_N2
hp = (x_CO2*hp_1+x_H2O*hp_2+x_O2*hp_3+x_N2*hp_4)/MM_prod
c_bar_p  = hp/(T_p1-T_p2)

ENDIF

ELSE

"Pure air case"
MM_a = x_air_O2*MM_O2+x_air_N2*MM_N2
ha_1 = (enthalpy(O2,T=T_p1)-enthalpy(O2, T=T_p2))*MM_O2
ha_2 = (enthalpy(N2,T=T_p1)-enthalpy(N2, T=T_p2))*MM_N2
ha = (x_air_O2*ha_1+x_air_N2*ha_2)/MM_a
c_bar_p  = ha/(T_p1-T_p2)
ENDIF

END

{--- End of the library functions copied from CSL-0005 ---}

"Engine data"
AU_gw=83.8    "jacket conductance product (gas to cooling water) [W/K]"
AU_wa=127.4   "water-to-environment conductance product [W/K]"
A_3=0.002072  "area A_3 of the original, in V_dot_3 = A_3*C_3 [m^2]"
eta_in_act=0.3277  "actual indicated efficiency (from its name) [-]"
T_m=39.79     "mean torque [N.m]"
i=1/2         "working cycles per revolution (1/2: four-stroke) [-]"
ncVs=5E-3     "engine displacement volume [m^3]"
f=0.055       "fuel-air ratio [kg of fuel/kg of air]"
t_a=20        "ambient air temperature [C]"
p=1E5         "ambient pressure [Pa]"
rpm=500       "engine speed [rpm]"
N_rot=rpm/60  "rotation rate [1/s]"
W_dot_sh=0    "shaft power [W] (the original imposes 0: see the note below)"
M_dot_w=0.9    "cooling water mass flow rate [kg/s]"
t_w_su=60     "cooling water supply temperature [C]"
LHV=50E6      "fuel lower heating value [J/kg]"

"In the original: the parametric table reduces the intake pressure p_2 to about
 1.8E4 Pa to cancel the shaft power (W_dot_sh = 0 imposed); p_2 = p_1 is kept
 as a display string in the equation window of the EES file, so P_2 is an input
 of the parametric run. Its value is taken from the stored solution."
"P_2 is not an input: p_2 = p_1 is kept as a display string in the equation window
 of the EES file, so the intake pressure after the throttle is solved by the model
 (17945.38 Pa in the stored solution of the original)."

"Comment of the original, kept as documentation of the other operating points:
 W_dot_sh = 90E3
 M_dot_f = 22/3600
 Q_dot_gw = 90E3
 W_dot_m = 10E3
 Q_dot_wa = 8E3"

"Nominal conditions (Figure V.16 of the textbook quoted by the original)"
t_1=t_a       "air temperature before the throttle [C]"
p_1=p         "air pressure before the throttle [Pa]"
t_2=t_1       "air temperature after the throttle [C] (the fuel is assumed to be
 at the same temperature as the air, as in the original)"

"States 1 to 5 (intake pressure loss, kinetic-energy balance)"
M_dot_g=M_dot_a+M_dot_f   "mass flow rate of the charge [kg/s]"
M_dot_f=f*M_dot_a         "fuel mass flow rate [kg/s]"
M_dot_g=V_dot_4/v_4       "charge mass flow rate from the swept volume [kg/s]"
V_dot_4=i*N_rot*ncVs      "volumetric flow rate of the engine [m^3/s]"
p_4=PRESSURE(Air,v=v_4,t=t_4)   "pressure from v_4 and t_4 [Pa]"
t_4=t_2       "temperature at state 4 [C]"
p_3=p_4
M_dot_g=V_dot_3/v_3       "charge mass flow rate from V_dot_3 [kg/s]"
V_dot_3=A_3*C_3           "volumetric flow rate at state 3 [m^3/s]"
v_3=VOLUME(Air,s=s_2,P=P_3)     "specific volume at state 3 [m^3/kg]"
s_2=ENTROPY(Air,T=T_2,P=P_2)    "specific entropy of the charge at state 2 [J/kg-K]"
c_p_2*(t_2-t_3)=C_3^2/2  "enthalpy drop between states 2 and 3 = C_3^2/2 [J/kg]"
c_p_2=CP(Air,T=T_2)       "specific heat of the charge [J/kg-K]"
"C_3 is the velocity at state 3 [m/s] of the kinetic-energy balance below; it follows
 from the equality of the two volumetric flows V_dot_3 = A_3*C_3 and V_dot_4 = i*N_rot*ncVs"
T_3=TEMPERATURE(Air,s=s_2,P=P_3) "temperature at state 3, isentropic path from state 2 [C]"
T_5=T_4
p_5=p_4

"Combustion chamber (energy balance of the reactants and the products, 25 C)"
Q_dot_1=M_dot_a*c_p_a*(25-t_5)  "heat received by the air [W]"
CALL cpbar(m,n,0,25,T_5:c_p_a,Q_4_a,x_a,e_min_a,e_a)  "mean c_p of the air [J/kg-K]"
m=1        "C of the CmHn fuel [-]"
n=4        "H of the CmHn fuel [-]"
Q_dot_2=M_dot_f*c_f*(25-t_5)  "heat received by the fuel [W]"
c_f=CP(CH4,T=T_5)   "specific heat of the fuel [J/kg-K]"
Q_dot_3=-M_dot_f*LHV   "power released by the fuel [W]"
Q_dot_4=0             "unburned CO losses [W] (air excess: none, as in the original)"
Q_dot_5=M_dot_g*c_p_g_6*(t_6-25)   "enthalpy of the combustion products [W]"
Q_dot_1+Q_dot_2+Q_dot_3+Q_dot_4+Q_dot_5=0
CALL cpbar(m,n,f,25,t_6:c_p_g_6,Q_4_6,x_6,e_min_6,e_6)  "mean c_p of the products
 between 25 C and t_6 [J/kg-K]"

"Expansion (shaft power from the enthalpy drop of the products)"
M_dot_g*c_p_g_67*(t_6-t_7)=W_dot_sh   "shaft power extracted [W]"
CALL cpbar(m,n,f,T_6,t_7:c_p_g_67,Q_4_67,x_67,e_min_67,e_67)  "mean c_p of the
 products between t_6 and t_7 [J/kg-K]"

"Cooling of the products by the jacket (eps-NTU)"
Q_dot_gw=epsilon_gw*C_dot_min_gw*(t_7-t_w_su)  "power transferred to the water [W]"
C_dot_min_gw=min(C_dot_g_78,C_dot_w)  "minimum heat capacity rate [W/K]"
C_dot_g_78=M_dot_g*c_p_g_78   "heat capacity rate of the products [W/K]"
CALL cpbar(m,n,f,T_7,t_8:c_p_g_78,Q_4_78,x_78,e_min_78,e_78)  "mean c_p of the
 products between t_7 and t_8 [J/kg-K]"
C_dot_w=M_dot_w*c_w          "heat capacity rate of the water [W/K]"
c_w=4187    "specific heat of the water [J/kg-K]"
Q_dot_gw=M_dot_g*c_p_g_78*(t_7-t_8)   "same power, from the products side"
epsilon_gw=(1-exp(-NTU_gw*(1-omega_gw)))/(1-omega_gw*exp(-NTU_gw*(1-omega_gw)))
NTU_gw=AU_gw/C_dot_min_gw    "number of transfer units of the jacket [-]"
omega_gw=C_dot_min_gw/C_dot_max_gw   "heat capacity rate ratio [-]"
C_dot_max_gw=max(C_dot_g_78,C_dot_w)  "maximum heat capacity rate [W/K]"
Q_dot_gw=C_dot_w*(t_w_ex_1-t_w_su)   "same power, from the water side: gives t_w_ex_1"

"Water-to-environment exchanger"
Q_dot_wa=epsilon_wa*C_dot_w*(t_w_ex_1-t_a)  "heat loss of the cooling water [W]"
Q_dot_wa=C_dot_w*(t_w_ex_1-t_w_ex)     "same power: gives the water exit temperature"
epsilon_wa=1-exp(-NTU_wa)
NTU_wa=AU_wa/C_dot_w   "number of transfer units of the water circuit [-]"

"Power and efficiencies"
W_dot_sh=W_dot_in_act-W_dot_p-W_dot_m   "shaft power [W]"
W_dot_p=V_dot_4*(p_1-p_4)  "power spent in the throttle (intake pressure drop) [W]"
eta_in_act=W_dot_in_act/(M_dot_f*LHV)  "actual indicated efficiency [-]"
eta_sh=W_dot_sh/(M_dot_f*LHV)   "shaft (mechanical) efficiency [-]"
W_dot_m=2*pi*N_rot*T_m   "power lost in the friction torque [W]"
